node_modules/
.DS_Store
# benchmark + experiment artifacts are large and regenerable
/bench/runs/
/spec/phase0-raw/

# The npm build output is regenerable. It is NOT only needed to publish: the docs site imports
# `@guml/core` through its `exports` map, which points at `dist/`, so a fresh clone cannot build the
# site until this exists. `docs`'s `build:deps` script regenerates it, which is why `pnpm --filter
# docs build` works on a machine that has never published anything. Deleting that script reproduces
# a green local build and a `Module not found: @guml/core` on the deployment host, because the only
# difference between the two is whether this directory happens to be lying around. The wasm is
# different — see below.
/packages/guml/dist/

# The built wasm IS committed: the docs site needs it at build time and its host
# has no Rust toolchain. Rebuild with `pnpm --filter guml build:wasm`.
